\p \v 13 \w So Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w and his troops|strong="H5971"\w* \w advanced|strong="H5066"\w* \w to fight|strong="H4421"\w* \w the Arameans|strong="H758"\w*, \w who fled|strong="H5127"\w* \w before him|strong="H6440"\w*. \v 14 \w When the Ammonites|strong="H1121"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w the Arameans|strong="H758"\w* \w had fled|strong="H5127"\w*, \w they too fled|strong="H5127"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w Abishai|strong="H52"\w*, \w and they entered|strong="H935"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*. \w So Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w returned|strong="H7725"\w* \w from fighting against|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Ammonites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and came|strong="H935"\w* \w to Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*.
\p \v 15 \w When the Arameans|strong="H758"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w they had been defeated|strong="H5062"\w* \w by|strong="H6440"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w they regrouped|strong="H622"\w*. \v 16 \w Hadadezer|strong="H1909"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w messengers to bring|strong="H3318"\w* \w more Arameans|strong="H758"\w* \w from beyond|strong="H5676"\w* \w the Euphrates|strong="H5104"\w*,\f + \fr 10:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \w and they came|strong="H935"\w* \w to Helam|strong="H2431"\w* \w with Shobach|strong="H7731"\w*\f + \fr 10:16 \fqa Shobach \ft is a variant of \fqa Shophach\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 19:16|1CH 19:16\ref*.\f* \w the commander|strong="H8269"\w* \w of Hadadezer’s|strong="H1909"\w* \w army|strong="H6635"\w* \w leading them|strong="H6440"\w*.
\p \v 17 \w When this was reported|strong="H5046"\w* \w to David|strong="H1732"\w*, \w he gathered|strong="H622"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w crossed|strong="H5674"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w*, \w and went|strong="H935"\w* \w to Helam|strong="H2431"\w*. \w Then the Arameans|strong="H758"\w* \w arrayed themselves|strong="H6186"\w* \w against|strong="H7122"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w and fought|strong="H3898"\w* \w against him|strong="H5973"\w*. \v 18 \w But the Arameans|strong="H758"\w* \w fled|strong="H5127"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w and David|strong="H1732"\w* \w killed|strong="H2026"\w* \w seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w hundred|strong="H3967"\w* \w charioteers|strong="H7393"\w* \w and forty|strong="H705"\w* \w thousand|strong="H505"\w* \w foot soldiers|strong="H6571"\w*.\f + \fr 10:18 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also \ref 1 Chronicles 19:18|1CH 19:18\ref*); Hebrew \fqa horsemen\f* \w He also struck down|strong="H5221"\w* \w Shobach|strong="H7731"\w* \w the commander|strong="H8269"\w* \w of their army|strong="H6635"\w*, \w who died|strong="H4191"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*.
\p \v 19 \w When all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the kings who were|strong="H4428"\w* \w subject|strong="H5650"\w* \w to Hadadezer|strong="H1909"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w they had been defeated|strong="H5062"\w* \w by|strong="H6440"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w they made peace|strong="H7999"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w and became subject to them|strong="H5647"\w*. \w So the Arameans|strong="H758"\w* \w were afraid|strong="H3372"\w* \w to help|strong="H3467"\w* \w the Ammonites|strong="H1121"\w* \w anymore|strong="H5750"\w*.
\c 11
\s1 David and Bathsheba
\p \v 1 \w In the spring|strong="H8666"\w*,\f + \fr 11:1 \ft Literally \fqa At the turn of the year\f* \w at the time when|strong="H6256"\w* \w kings|strong="H4397"\w* \w march out to war|strong="H3318"\w*, \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w sent out|strong="H7971"\w* \w Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w his servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w with|strong="H853"\w* \w the whole army|strong="H3605"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \w They destroyed|strong="H7843"\w* \w the Ammonites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and besieged|strong="H6696"\w* \w Rabbah|strong="H7237"\w*, \w but David|strong="H1732"\w* \w remained|strong="H3427"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*.
\p \v 2 \w One evening|strong="H6153"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w got up|strong="H6965"\w* \w from|strong="H5921"\w* \w his bed|strong="H4904"\w* \w and strolled around|strong="H1980"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the roof|strong="H1406"\w* \w of the palace|strong="H1004"\w*. \w And from|strong="H5921"\w* \w the roof|strong="H1406"\w* \w he saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w a woman|strong="H802"\w* \w bathing|strong="H7364"\w*— \w a very|strong="H3966"\w* \w beautiful|strong="H2896"\w* \w woman|strong="H802"\w*. \v 3 \w So David|strong="H1732"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w and inquired|strong="H1875"\w* \w about the woman|strong="H802"\w*, \w and he was told|strong="H559"\w*, “\w This|strong="H2063"\w* \w is Bathsheba|strong="H1339"\w*, \w the daughter|strong="H1323"\w* \w of Eliam|strong="H463"\w*\f + \fr 11:3 \fqa Eliam \ft is a variant of \fqa Ammiel\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 3:5|1CH 3:5\ref*.\f* \w and the wife|strong="H802"\w* \w of Uriah|strong="H223"\w* \w the Hittite|strong="H2850"\w*.”
\p \v 4 \w Then David|strong="H1732"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w messengers|strong="H4397"\w* \w to get her|strong="H3947"\w*, \w and when she came|strong="H935"\w* \w to him|strong="H413"\w*, \w he slept|strong="H7901"\w* \w with her|strong="H5973"\w*. (\w Now she|strong="H1931"\w* \w had just purified herself|strong="H6942"\w* \w from her uncleanness|strong="H2932"\w*.) \w Then she returned|strong="H7725"\w* \w home|strong="H1004"\w*. \v 5 \w And the woman|strong="H802"\w* \w conceived|strong="H2029"\w* \w and sent word|strong="H7971"\w* \w to David|strong="H1732"\w*, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, “\w I|strong="H595"\w* \w am pregnant|strong="H2030"\w*.”
\p \v 6 \w At this, David|strong="H1732"\w* \w sent orders|strong="H7971"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joab|strong="H3097"\w*: “\w Send|strong="H7971"\w* \w me|strong="H413"\w* \w Uriah|strong="H223"\w* \w the Hittite|strong="H2850"\w*.” \w So Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w him|strong="H223"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w*.
