\p \v 25 \w Then David|strong="H1732"\w* \w told|strong="H559"\w* \w the messenger|strong="H4397"\w*, “\w Say|strong="H559"\w* \w this|strong="H3541"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joab|strong="H3097"\w*: ‘\w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w let this|strong="H2088"\w* \w matter|strong="H1697"\w* \w upset|strong="H7489"\w* \w you|strong="H5869"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w the sword|strong="H2719"\w* \w devours|strong="H398"\w* \w one|strong="H2088"\w* \w as well as another|strong="H2090"\w*. \w Strengthen|strong="H2388"\w* \w your attack|strong="H4421"\w* \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w and demolish it|strong="H2040"\w*.’ \w Encourage him with these words|strong="H2388"\w*.”
\s1 David Marries Bathsheba
\p \v 26 \w When Uriah’s|strong="H223"\w* \w wife|strong="H802"\w* \w heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w her husband|strong="H376"\w* \w was dead|strong="H4191"\w*, \w she mourned|strong="H5594"\w* \w for|strong="H5921"\w* \w him|strong="H1167"\w*. \v 27 \w And when the time of mourning|strong="H60"\w* \w was over|strong="H5674"\w*, \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w had her brought|strong="H622"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w his house|strong="H1004"\w*, \w and she became|strong="H1961"\w* his \w wife|strong="H802"\w* \w and bore|strong="H3205"\w* him \w a son|strong="H1121"\w*.
\p \w But the thing|strong="H1697"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w had done|strong="H6213"\w* \w was evil|strong="H7489"\w* \w in the sight|strong="H5869"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\c 12
\s1 Nathan Rebukes David
\r (\ref Psalm 51:1–19|PSA 51:1-19\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w Nathan|strong="H5416"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w*, \w and when he arrived|strong="H935"\w*, \w he said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w There were|strong="H1961"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w in a certain|strong="H259"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w rich|strong="H6223"\w* \w and the other|strong="H259"\w* \w poor|strong="H7326"\w*. \v 2 \w The rich|strong="H6223"\w* \w man had|strong="H1961"\w* \w a great number of|strong="H7235"\w* \w sheep|strong="H6629"\w* \w and cattle|strong="H1241"\w*, \v 3 \w but the poor|strong="H7326"\w* \w man had nothing|strong="H369"\w* \w except|strong="H3588"\w* \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w small|strong="H6996"\w* \w ewe lamb|strong="H3535"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w he had bought|strong="H7069"\w*. \w He raised it|strong="H2421"\w*, \w and it grew up|strong="H1431"\w* \w with him|strong="H5973"\w* \w and his children|strong="H1121"\w*. \w It shared|strong="H3162"\w* \w his food|strong="H6595"\w* \w and drank|strong="H8354"\w* \w from his cup|strong="H3563"\w*; \w it slept|strong="H7901"\w* \w in his arms|strong="H2436"\w*\f + \fr 12:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa in his bosom\ft ; also in verse 8\f* \w and was|strong="H1961"\w* \w like a daughter|strong="H1323"\w* to him.
\p \v 4 \w Now a traveler|strong="H1982"\w* \w came|strong="H935"\w* \w to the rich|strong="H6223"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w*, \w who refrained from taking|strong="H3947"\w* \w one of his own sheep|strong="H6629"\w* \w or cattle|strong="H1241"\w* \w to prepare|strong="H6213"\w* \w for the traveler|strong="H732"\w* \w who had come|strong="H935"\w* to him. \w Instead, he took|strong="H3947"\w* \w the poor|strong="H7326"\w* \w man’s|strong="H376"\w* \w lamb|strong="H3535"\w* \w and prepared it|strong="H6213"\w* \w for his guest|strong="H376"\w*.”
