\p \v 18 \w On the seventh|strong="H7637"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w the child|strong="H3206"\w* \w died|strong="H4191"\w*. \w But David’s|strong="H1732"\w* \w servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w were afraid|strong="H3372"\w* \w to tell|strong="H5046"\w* him \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w the child|strong="H3206"\w* \w was dead|strong="H4191"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w they said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Look|strong="H2009"\w*, \w while the child|strong="H3206"\w* \w was alive|strong="H2416"\w*, \w we spoke|strong="H1696"\w* \w to him|strong="H413"\w*, \w and he would not|strong="H3808"\w* \w listen to us|strong="H8085"\w*. \w So how|strong="H349"\w* \w can we tell|strong="H559"\w* \w him|strong="H413"\w* \w the child|strong="H3206"\w* \w is dead|strong="H4191"\w*? \w He may even harm himself|strong="H6213"\w*.”
