\s1 Absalom’s Revenge on Amnon
\p \v 23 \w Two years later|strong="H8141"\w*, \w when Absalom’s|strong="H53"\w* \w sheepshearers|strong="H1494"\w* \w were|strong="H1961"\w* \w at Baal-hazor|strong="H1178"\w* \w near|strong="H5973"\w* \w Ephraim|strong="H669"\w*, \w he|strong="H53"\w* \w invited|strong="H7121"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w*. \v 24 \w And he|strong="H53"\w* \w went|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Your servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w has just|strong="H2009"\w* \w hired shearers|strong="H1494"\w*. \w Will the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and his servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w please|strong="H4994"\w* \w come|strong="H1980"\w* \w with|strong="H5973"\w* \w me|strong="H5650"\w*?”
\p \v 25 “\w No|strong="H408"\w*, \w my son|strong="H1121"\w*,” \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w we should not|strong="H408"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w go|strong="H1980"\w*, \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w we would be a burden|strong="H3513"\w* \w to you|strong="H5921"\w*.” \w Although Absalom urged|strong="H6555"\w* him, \w he was not|strong="H3808"\w* \w willing|strong="H14"\w* \w to go|strong="H1980"\w*, \w but gave him his blessing|strong="H1288"\w*.
