\p \v 32 \w But Jonadab|strong="H3122"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of David’s|strong="H1732"\w* \w brother|strong="H251"\w* \w Shimeah|strong="H8093"\w*, \w spoke up|strong="H6030"\w*: “\w My lord|strong="H113"\w* \w must not|strong="H408"\w* \w think|strong="H559"\w* \w they have killed|strong="H4191"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w only|strong="H905"\w* \w Amnon|strong="H550"\w* \w is dead|strong="H4191"\w*. \w In fact|strong="H3588"\w*, \w Absalom|strong="H53"\w* \w has planned this|strong="H7760"\w* \w since the day|strong="H3117"\w* \w Amnon violated|strong="H6031"\w* \w his sister|strong="H269"\w* \w Tamar|strong="H8559"\w*. \v 33 \w So now|strong="H6258"\w*, \w my lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w do not|strong="H408"\w* \w take|strong="H7760"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w heart|strong="H3820"\w* \w the report that|strong="H1697"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w are dead|strong="H4191"\w*. \w Only|strong="H905"\w* \w Amnon|strong="H550"\w* \w is dead|strong="H4191"\w*.”
\s1 Absalom Flees to Geshur
\p \v 34 \w Meanwhile, Absalom|strong="H53"\w* \w had fled|strong="H1272"\w*. \w When the young man|strong="H5288"\w* \w standing watch|strong="H6822"\w* \w looked up|strong="H5375"\w*, \w he saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w many|strong="H7227"\w* \w people|strong="H5971"\w* \w coming|strong="H1980"\w* \w down the road|strong="H1870"\w* \w west of him|strong="H310"\w*,\f + \fr 13:34 \ft Or \fqa behind him\f* \w along the side|strong="H6654"\w* \w of the hill. And the watchman went and reported to the king, “I see men coming from the direction of Horonaim, along the side of the hill|strong="H2022"\w*.”\f + \fr 13:34 \ft LXX; Hebrew does not include \fqa And the watchman...\ft .\f*
