\p \v 5 “\w What|strong="H4100"\w* troubles you?” \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w asked|strong="H559"\w* her.
\p “\w Indeed|strong="H61"\w*,” \w she said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w I am|strong="H589"\w* \w a widow|strong="H490"\w*, \w for my husband|strong="H376"\w* \w is dead|strong="H4191"\w*. \v 6 \w And your maidservant|strong="H8198"\w* \w had two|strong="H8147"\w* \w sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w who|strong="H8147"\w* \w were fighting|strong="H5327"\w* \w in the field|strong="H7704"\w* \w with no|strong="H369"\w* \w one to separate|strong="H5337"\w* \w them|strong="H996"\w*, \w and one|strong="H259"\w* \w struck|strong="H5221"\w* \w the other|strong="H259"\w* \w and killed|strong="H4191"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w*. \v 7 \w Now|strong="H2009"\w* \w the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w clan|strong="H4940"\w* \w has risen up|strong="H6965"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w your maidservant|strong="H8198"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w Hand over|strong="H5414"\w* \w the one who struck down|strong="H5221"\w* \w his brother|strong="H251"\w*, \w that we may put him to death|strong="H4191"\w* \w for the life|strong="H5315"\w* \w of the brother|strong="H251"\w* \w whom|strong="H834"\w* \w he killed|strong="H2026"\w*. \w Then we will cut off|strong="H8045"\w* \w the heir|strong="H3423"\w* \w as well|strong="H1571"\w*!’ \w So they would extinguish|strong="H3518"\w* \w my one remaining|strong="H7604"\w* \w ember|strong="H1513"\w* \w by not|strong="H1115"\w* \w preserving|strong="H7760"\w* \w my husband’s|strong="H376"\w* \w name|strong="H8034"\w* \w or posterity|strong="H7611"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the earth|strong="H127"\w*.”
\p \v 8 “\w Go|strong="H1980"\w* \w home|strong="H1004"\w*,” \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the woman|strong="H802"\w*, “\w and I|strong="H589"\w* \w will give orders|strong="H6680"\w* \w on your behalf|strong="H5921"\w*.”
