\s1 Hushai’s Warning Saves David
\r (\ref Psalm 55:1–23|PSA 55:1-23\ref*)
\p \v 15 \w So Hushai|strong="H2365"\w* \w told|strong="H559"\w* \w Zadok|strong="H6659"\w* \w and Abiathar|strong="H54"\w*, \w the priests|strong="H3548"\w*, “\w This is what|strong="H2063"\w* \w Ahithophel|strong="H302"\w* \w has advised|strong="H3289"\w* \w Absalom|strong="H53"\w* \w and the elders|strong="H2205"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w and this is what|strong="H2063"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w have advised|strong="H3289"\w*. \v 16 \w Now|strong="H6258"\w* \w send|strong="H7971"\w* \w quickly|strong="H4120"\w* \w and tell|strong="H5046"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w*, ‘\w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w spend|strong="H3885"\w* \w the night|strong="H3915"\w* \w at the fords|strong="H6160"\w* \w of the wilderness|strong="H4057"\w*, \w but|strong="H1571"\w* \w be sure to cross over|strong="H5674"\w*. \w Otherwise|strong="H6435"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w with him|strong="H854"\w* \w will be swallowed up|strong="H1104"\w*.’”
