\p \v 18 \w During his lifetime|strong="H2416"\w*, \w Absalom|strong="H53"\w* \w had set up|strong="H5324"\w* for himself \w a pillar|strong="H4678"\w* \w in the King’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w Valley|strong="H6010"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w he had said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w I have no|strong="H369"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w to|strong="H5668"\w* \w preserve the memory|strong="H2142"\w* \w of my name|strong="H8034"\w*.” \w So he gave|strong="H7121"\w* \w the pillar|strong="H4678"\w* \w his name|strong="H8034"\w*, \w and to|strong="H5704"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w it is called|strong="H7121"\w* \w Absalom’s|strong="H53"\w* \w Monument|strong="H3027"\w*.
\s1 David Mourns for Absalom
\p \v 19 \w Then Ahimaaz|strong="H290"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zadok|strong="H6659"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Please|strong="H4994"\w* \w let me run|strong="H7323"\w* \w and tell the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w the good news|strong="H1319"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has avenged him|strong="H8199"\w* \w of|strong="H3027"\w* \w his enemies|strong="H341"\w*.”
