\p \w So Ahimaaz|strong="H290"\w* \w ran|strong="H7323"\w* \w by way|strong="H1870"\w* \w of the plain|strong="H3603"\w*\f + \fr 18:23 \ft That is, the plain of the Jordan\f* \w and outran|strong="H5674"\w* \w the Cushite|strong="H3569"\w*.
\p \v 24 \w Now David|strong="H1732"\w* \w was sitting|strong="H3427"\w* \w between|strong="H996"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w gates|strong="H8179"\w* \w when the watchman|strong="H6822"\w* \w went up|strong="H1980"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the roof|strong="H1406"\w* \w of the gateway|strong="H8179"\w* \w by|strong="H413"\w* \w the wall|strong="H2346"\w*, \w looked out|strong="H5375"\w*, \w and saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w a man|strong="H376"\w* \w running alone|strong="H7323"\w*. \v 25 \w So he|strong="H6822"\w* \w called out|strong="H7121"\w* \w and told|strong="H5046"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*.
