\s1 David Restored as King
\p \v 8 \w So the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w got up|strong="H6965"\w* \w and sat|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the gate|strong="H8179"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w were told|strong="H5046"\w*: “\w Behold|strong="H2009"\w*, \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w is sitting|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the gate|strong="H8179"\w*.” \w So they|strong="H5971"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w came|strong="H935"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*.
\p \w Meanwhile, the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w* \w had fled|strong="H5127"\w*, \w each man|strong="H376"\w* \w to his home|strong="H168"\w*. \v 9 \w And|strong="H1961"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w throughout|strong="H3605"\w* \w the tribes|strong="H7626"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w were arguing|strong="H1777"\w*, “\w The king|strong="H4428"\w* \w rescued us|strong="H5337"\w* \w from the hand|strong="H3709"\w* \w of our enemies|strong="H341"\w* \w and|strong="H1931"\w* \w delivered us|strong="H4422"\w* \w from the hand|strong="H3709"\w* \w of the Philistines|strong="H6430"\w*, \w but now|strong="H6258"\w* \w he has fled|strong="H1272"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w because|strong="H5921"\w* \w of Absalom|strong="H53"\w*. \v 10 \w But Absalom|strong="H53"\w*, \w the man|strong="H834"\w* \w we anointed|strong="H4886"\w* \w over us|strong="H5921"\w*, \w has died|strong="H4191"\w* \w in battle|strong="H4421"\w*. \w So|strong="H6258"\w* \w why|strong="H4100"\w* \w do you|strong="H859"\w* \w say nothing|strong="H2790"\w* \w about restoring|strong="H7725"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*?”
