\s1 David’s Kindness to Barzillai
\p \v 31 \w Now Barzillai|strong="H1271"\w* \w the Gileadite|strong="H1569"\w* \w had come down|strong="H3381"\w* \w from Rogelim|strong="H7274"\w* \w to cross|strong="H5674"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and send him on his way|strong="H7971"\w* \w from there|strong="H3383"\w*. \v 32 \w Barzillai|strong="H1271"\w* \w was quite|strong="H3966"\w* \w old|strong="H2204"\w*, \w eighty|strong="H8084"\w* \w years|strong="H8141"\w* \w of age|strong="H1121"\w*, \w and since|strong="H3588"\w* \w he was a very|strong="H3966"\w* \w wealthy|strong="H1419"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w*, \w he|strong="H1931"\w* \w had provided|strong="H3557"\w* \w for the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w while he stayed|strong="H7871"\w* \w in Mahanaim|strong="H4266"\w*.
\p \v 33 \w The king|strong="H4428"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Barzillai|strong="H1271"\w*, “\w Cross over|strong="H5674"\w* \w with me|strong="H854"\w*, \w and I will provide|strong="H3557"\w* \w for you|strong="H853"\w* \w at my side|strong="H5978"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*.”
\p \v 34 \w But Barzillai|strong="H1271"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w How many|strong="H4100"\w* \w years|strong="H3117"\w* \w of my life remain|strong="H2416"\w*, \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w I should go up|strong="H5927"\w* \w to Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*? \v 35 \w I am|strong="H595"\w* \w now|strong="H3117"\w* \w eighty|strong="H8084"\w* \w years old|strong="H1121"\w*. \w Can I discern|strong="H3045"\w* \w what is good|strong="H2896"\w* \w and what is not|strong="H7451"\w*? \w Can your servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w taste|strong="H2938"\w* \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w he eats|strong="H398"\w* \w or drinks|strong="H8354"\w*? \w Can I still|strong="H5750"\w* \w hear|strong="H8085"\w* \w the voice|strong="H6963"\w* \w of singing men|strong="H7891"\w* \w and women|strong="H7891"\w*? \w Why|strong="H4100"\w* \w should your servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w be|strong="H1961"\w* \w an added|strong="H5750"\w* \w burden|strong="H4853"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w my lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*?
\p \v 36 \w Your servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w will go with|strong="H854"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w only a short distance|strong="H4592"\w* \w past|strong="H5674"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w*; \w why|strong="H4100"\w* \w should the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w repay me|strong="H1580"\w* \w with such|strong="H2063"\w* \w a reward|strong="H1578"\w*? \v 37 \w Please|strong="H4994"\w* \w let your servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w return|strong="H7725"\w*, \w that I may die|strong="H4191"\w* \w in my own city|strong="H5892"\w* \w near|strong="H5973"\w* \w the tomb|strong="H6913"\w* \w of my father|strong="H1"\w* \w and mother|strong="H517"\w*. \w But here|strong="H2009"\w* \w is your servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w Chimham|strong="H3643"\w*. \w Let him cross over|strong="H5674"\w* \w with|strong="H5973"\w* \w my lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w and do|strong="H6213"\w* for him \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w is good|strong="H2895"\w* \w in your sight|strong="H5869"\w*.”
\p \v 38 \w The king|strong="H4428"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Chimham|strong="H3643"\w* \w will cross over|strong="H5674"\w* \w with me|strong="H854"\w*, \w and I|strong="H589"\w* \w will do|strong="H6213"\w* for him \w what is good|strong="H2896"\w* \w in your sight|strong="H5869"\w*, \w and I will do|strong="H6213"\w* for you \w whatever|strong="H3605"\w* \w you desire|strong="H977"\w* \w of me|strong="H5921"\w*.”
