\p \v 43 “\w We have ten|strong="H6235"\w* \w shares|strong="H3027"\w* \w in the king|strong="H4428"\w*,” \w answered|strong="H6030"\w* \w the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, “\w so we have more claim|strong="H1571"\w* \w to David|strong="H1732"\w* \w than you|strong="H4480"\w*. \w Why|strong="H4069"\w* \w then do you despise us|strong="H7043"\w*? \w Were we not|strong="H3808"\w* \w the first|strong="H7223"\w* \w to speak|strong="H1697"\w* \w of restoring|strong="H7725"\w* \w our king|strong="H4428"\w*?”
\p \w But the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w spoke more fiercely|strong="H7185"\w* \w than|strong="H1697"\w* \w the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*.
\c 20
\s1 Sheba’s Rebellion
\p \v 1 \w Now a worthless|strong="H1100"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w* \w named|strong="H8034"\w* \w Sheba|strong="H7652"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Bichri|strong="H1075"\w*, \w a Benjamite|strong="H3228"\w*, \w happened|strong="H7122"\w* \w to be there|strong="H8033"\w*, \w and he blew|strong="H8628"\w* \w the ram’s horn|strong="H7782"\w* \w and shouted|strong="H559"\w*:
\b 
\q1 “\w We have no|strong="H369"\w* \w share|strong="H2506"\w* \w in David|strong="H1732"\w*,
\q2 \w no|strong="H3808"\w* \w inheritance|strong="H5159"\w* \w in Jesse’s|strong="H3448"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w*.
\q1 \w Every man|strong="H376"\w* \w to his tent|strong="H168"\w*,
\q2 \w O Israel|strong="H3478"\w*!”
\p \v 2 \w So all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w deserted|strong="H5927"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w to follow|strong="H310"\w* \w Sheba|strong="H7652"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Bichri|strong="H1075"\w*. \w But the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w stayed by|strong="H1692"\w* \w their king|strong="H4428"\w* \w all the way|strong="H5704"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w* \w to Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w When David|strong="H1732"\w* \w returned|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w his palace|strong="H1004"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*, \w he|strong="H4428"\w* \w took|strong="H3947"\w* \w the ten|strong="H6235"\w* \w concubines|strong="H6370"\w* \w he had left|strong="H5117"\w* \w to take care of|strong="H8104"\w* \w the palace|strong="H1004"\w*, \w and he placed them|strong="H5414"\w* \w in a house|strong="H1004"\w* \w under guard|strong="H4931"\w*. \w He provided for them|strong="H3557"\w*, \w but he no longer|strong="H3808"\w* \w slept with|strong="H413"\w* \w them|strong="H935"\w*. \w They were|strong="H1961"\w* \w confined|strong="H6887"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w the day|strong="H3117"\w* \w of their death|strong="H4191"\w*, \w living|strong="H2424"\w* \w as widows|strong="H491"\w*.
