\p “\w Listen|strong="H8085"\w* \w to the words|strong="H1697"\w* \w of your servant|strong="H519"\w*,” \w she said|strong="H559"\w*.
\p “\w I am|strong="H595"\w* \w listening|strong="H8085"\w*,” \w he answered|strong="H559"\w*.
\p \v 18 \w Then the woman said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Long ago|strong="H7223"\w* \w they used to say|strong="H1696"\w*, ‘\w Seek counsel|strong="H7592"\w* \w at Abel|strong="H59"\w*,’ \w and that is how|strong="H3651"\w* \w disputes were settled|strong="H8552"\w*. \v 19 \w I am|strong="H595"\w* \w among the peaceable|strong="H7999"\w* \w and faithful|strong="H529"\w* \w in Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w but you are|strong="H859"\w* \w trying|strong="H1245"\w* \w to destroy|strong="H4191"\w* \w a city|strong="H5892"\w* \w that is a mother|strong="H517"\w* \w in Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \w Why|strong="H4100"\w* \w would you swallow up|strong="H1104"\w* \w the LORD’s|strong="H3068"\w* \w inheritance|strong="H5159"\w*?”
\p \v 20 “\w Far be it|strong="H2486"\w*!” \w Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w declared|strong="H559"\w*. “\w Far be it|strong="H2486"\w* from me \w to|strong="H518"\w* \w swallow up|strong="H1104"\w* \w or|strong="H518"\w* \w destroy|strong="H7843"\w*! \v 21 \w That is|strong="H1697"\w* \w not|strong="H3808"\w* \w the case|strong="H3651"\w*. \w But|strong="H3588"\w* \w a man|strong="H376"\w* \w named|strong="H8034"\w* \w Sheba|strong="H7652"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Bichri|strong="H1075"\w*, \w from the hill country|strong="H2022"\w* \w of Ephraim|strong="H669"\w*, \w has lifted|strong="H5375"\w* \w up his hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w against the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w against David|strong="H1732"\w*. \w Deliver|strong="H5414"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w alone|strong="H905"\w*, \w and I will depart|strong="H1980"\w* \w from|strong="H5921"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*.”
