\s1 David’s Mighty Men
\r (\ref 1 Chronicles 11:10–47|1CH 11:10-47\ref*)
\p \v 8 \w These|strong="H428"\w* \w are the names|strong="H8034"\w* \w of David’s|strong="H1732"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H1368"\w*:
\b 
\li1 \w Josheb-basshebeth|strong="H3429"\w* \w the Tahchemonite|strong="H8461"\w*\f + \fr 23:8 \fqa Tahchemonite \ft is probably a variant of \fqa Hachmonite\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 11:11|1CH 11:11\ref*.\f* \w was chief|strong="H7218"\w* \w of the Three|strong="H7991"\w*.\f + \fr 23:8 \ft Or \fqa chief among the captains\f* \w He|strong="H1931"\w* \w wielded|strong="H5722"\w* \w his spear|strong="H6112"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w*\f + \fr 23:8 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also \ref 1 Chronicles 11:11|1CH 11:11\ref*); Hebrew \fqa He was called Adino the Eznite because of\f* \w eight|strong="H8083"\w* \w hundred men|strong="H3967"\w*, \w whom he killed|strong="H2491"\w* \w at one|strong="H259"\w* \w time|strong="H6471"\w*.
\li1 \v 9 \w Next in command was|strong="H310"\w* \w Eleazar|strong="H499"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Dodo|strong="H1734"\w*\f + \fr 23:9 \fqa Dodo \ft is a variant of \fqa Dodai\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 27:4|1CH 27:4\ref*.\f* \w the Ahohite|strong="H266"\w*. \w As one of the three|strong="H7969"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H1368"\w*, \w he went with|strong="H5973"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w to taunt|strong="H2778"\w* \w the Philistines|strong="H6430"\w* \w who had gathered|strong="H622"\w* \w for battle|strong="H4421"\w* \w at Pas-dammim|strong="H8033"\w*. \w The men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w retreated|strong="H5927"\w*, \v 10 \w but Eleazar|strong="H1931"\w* \w stood his ground|strong="H6965"\w* \w and struck|strong="H5221"\w* \w the Philistines|strong="H6430"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w his hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w grew weary|strong="H3021"\w* \w and stuck|strong="H1692"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w his sword|strong="H2719"\w*. \w The LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w brought about|strong="H6213"\w* \w a great|strong="H1419"\w* \w victory|strong="H8668"\w* \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*. \w Then the troops|strong="H5971"\w* \w returned|strong="H7725"\w* \w to him|strong="H310"\w*, \w but only|strong="H389"\w* \w to plunder the dead|strong="H6584"\w*.
\li1 \v 11 \w And after him|strong="H310"\w* \w was Shammah|strong="H8037"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Agee|strong="H89"\w* \w the Hararite|strong="H2043"\w*. \w When the Philistines|strong="H6430"\w* \w had banded together|strong="H622"\w* \w near|strong="H3896"\w* \w a field|strong="H2513"\w* \w full of|strong="H4392"\w* \w lentils|strong="H5742"\w*, \w Israel’s troops|strong="H5971"\w* \w fled|strong="H5127"\w* \w from|strong="H6440"\w* \w them|strong="H6430"\w*. \v 12 \w But Shammah took his stand|strong="H3320"\w* \w in the middle|strong="H8432"\w* \w of the field|strong="H2513"\w*, \w defended it|strong="H5337"\w*, \w and struck down|strong="H5221"\w* \w the Philistines|strong="H6430"\w*. \w So the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w brought about|strong="H6213"\w* \w a great|strong="H1419"\w* \w victory|strong="H8668"\w*.
\p \v 13 \w At|strong="H413"\w* \w harvest time|strong="H7105"\w*, \w three|strong="H7970"\w* \w of the thirty|strong="H7970"\w* \w chief men|strong="H7218"\w* \w went down|strong="H3381"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the cave|strong="H4631"\w* \w of Adullam|strong="H5725"\w*, \w while a company|strong="H2416"\w* \w of Philistines|strong="H6430"\w* \w was encamped|strong="H2583"\w* \w in the Valley|strong="H6010"\w* \w of Rephaim|strong="H7497"\w*. \v 14 \w At that time|strong="H227"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w was in the stronghold|strong="H4686"\w*, \w and the garrison|strong="H4673"\w* \w of the Philistines|strong="H6430"\w* \w was at Bethlehem|strong="H1035"\w*. \v 15 \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w longed for water|strong="H183"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Oh, that someone|strong="H4310"\w* \w would get me a drink|strong="H8248"\w* \w of water|strong="H4325"\w* \w from the well|strong="H877"\w* \w near the gate|strong="H8179"\w* \w of Bethlehem|strong="H1035"\w*!”
\p \v 16 \w So the three|strong="H7969"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H1368"\w* \w broke|strong="H1234"\w* \w through the Philistine|strong="H6430"\w* \w camp|strong="H4264"\w*, \w drew|strong="H7579"\w* \w water|strong="H4325"\w* \w from the well|strong="H877"\w* \w near the gate|strong="H8179"\w* \w of Bethlehem|strong="H1035"\w*, \w and brought it|strong="H935"\w* \w back to|strong="H413"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w*. \w But he refused|strong="H3808"\w* \w to drink it|strong="H8354"\w*; \w instead , he poured it out|strong="H5258"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \v 17 \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Far be it|strong="H2486"\w* from me, \w O LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w to do|strong="H6213"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w*! \w Is this not the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w of the men|strong="H582"\w* \w who risked their lives|strong="H5315"\w*?” \w So he refused|strong="H3808"\w* \w to drink it|strong="H8354"\w*.
\p \w Such|strong="H428"\w* \w were the exploits|strong="H6213"\w* \w of the three|strong="H7969"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H1368"\w*.
\p \v 18 \w Now Abishai|strong="H52"\w*, \w the brother|strong="H251"\w* \w of Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w and son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zeruiah|strong="H6870"\w*, \w was chief|strong="H7218"\w* \w of the Three|strong="H7992"\w*,\f + \fr 23:18 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts (see also \ref 1 Chronicles 11:20|1CH 11:20\ref*); two Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac \fqa the Thirty\f* \w and he|strong="H1931"\w* \w wielded|strong="H5782"\w* \w his spear|strong="H2595"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w three|strong="H7969"\w* \w hundred men|strong="H3967"\w*, \w killed them|strong="H2491"\w*, and won \w a name|strong="H8034"\w* \w along with the Three|strong="H7969"\w*. \v 19 \w Was he not|strong="H3588"\w* \w more honored|strong="H3513"\w* \w than|strong="H4480"\w* \w the Three|strong="H7969"\w*?\f + \fr 23:19 \ft Hebrew; Syriac \fqa the Thirty\f* \w And he became|strong="H1961"\w* their \w commander|strong="H8269"\w*, \w even though he was not|strong="H3808"\w* \w included|strong="H935"\w* \w among the Three|strong="H7969"\w*.
