\c 24
\s1 David’s Military Census
\r (\ref Exodus 30:11–16|EXO 30:11-16\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 21:1–6|1CH 21:1-6\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w Again|strong="H3254"\w* \w the anger|strong="H639"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w burned|strong="H2734"\w* \w against Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w and He stirred up|strong="H5496"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* against them, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Go|strong="H1980"\w* \w and take a census|strong="H4487"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w and Judah|strong="H3063"\w*.”
\p \v 2 \w So the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w the commander|strong="H8269"\w* \w of his army|strong="H2428"\w*, \w who was|strong="H834"\w* \w with him|strong="H854"\w*,\f + \fr 24:2 \ft LXX \fqa to Joab and the army commanders with him\f* “\w Go|strong="H7751"\w* \w now|strong="H4994"\w* \w throughout|strong="H3605"\w* \w the tribes|strong="H7626"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w from Dan|strong="H1835"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w Beersheba|strong="H884"\w* \w and register|strong="H6485"\w* \w the troops|strong="H5971"\w*, \w so that I may know|strong="H3045"\w* \w their number|strong="H4557"\w*.”
\p \v 3 \w But Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, “\w May the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w your God|strong="H430"\w* \w multiply|strong="H3254"\w* \w the troops|strong="H5971"\w* \w a hundred|strong="H3967"\w* \w times|strong="H6471"\w* over, \w and may the eyes|strong="H5869"\w* \w of my lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w see it|strong="H7200"\w*. \w But why|strong="H4100"\w* \w does my lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w want|strong="H2654"\w* \w to do such|strong="H2088"\w* \w a thing|strong="H1697"\w*?”
\p \v 4 \w Nevertheless , the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w word|strong="H1697"\w* \w prevailed|strong="H2388"\w* \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w and against|strong="H5921"\w* \w the commanders|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the army|strong="H2428"\w*. \w So Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w and the commanders|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the army|strong="H2428"\w* \w departed|strong="H3318"\w* \w from the presence|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w to register|strong="H6485"\w* \w the troops|strong="H5971"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*.
\p \v 5 \w They crossed|strong="H5674"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w near Aroer|strong="H6177"\w*, \w south|strong="H3225"\w* \w of the town|strong="H5892"\w* \w in the middle|strong="H8432"\w* \w of the valley|strong="H5158"\w*, \w and proceeded toward Gad|strong="H1410"\w* \w and Jazer|strong="H3270"\w*. \v 6 \w Then they went|strong="H935"\w* \w to Gilead|strong="H1568"\w* \w and|strong="H413"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Tahtim-hodshi|strong="H8483"\w*,\f + \fr 24:6 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa to Gilead and to the land of the Hittites\f* \w and|strong="H935"\w* \w on to Dan-jaan|strong="H1842"\w* \w and around|strong="H5439"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Sidon|strong="H6721"\w*. \v 7 \w They went|strong="H935"\w* \w toward the fortress|strong="H4013"\w* \w of Tyre|strong="H6865"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w of the Hivites|strong="H2340"\w* \w and Canaanites|strong="H3669"\w*. \w Finally, they went on|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Negev|strong="H5045"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*,\f + \fr 24:7 \ft Or \fqa to the south of Judah\f* \w to Beersheba|strong="H884"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w At the end|strong="H7097"\w* \w of nine|strong="H8672"\w* \w months|strong="H2320"\w* \w and twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w*, \w having gone|strong="H7751"\w* \w through the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w land|strong="H776"\w*, \w they returned|strong="H935"\w* \w to Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*. \v 9 \w And Joab|strong="H3097"\w* \w reported|strong="H5414"\w* \w to the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w the total|strong="H4557"\w* \w number|strong="H4662"\w* \w of the troops|strong="H5971"\w*. \w In Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w there were|strong="H1961"\w* \w 800,000|strong="H8083"\w* \w men|strong="H376"\w* \w of valor|strong="H2428"\w* \w who drew|strong="H8025"\w* \w the sword|strong="H2719"\w*, \w and|strong="H376"\w* \w in Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w there were 500,000|strong="H2568"\w*.
\s1 Judgment for David’s Sin
\r (\ref 1 Chronicles 21:7–13|1CH 21:7-13\ref*)
\p \v 10 \w After|strong="H310"\w* \w David had numbered|strong="H5608"\w* \w the troops|strong="H5971"\w*, \w his|strong="H1732"\w* \w conscience|strong="H3820"\w* \w was stricken|strong="H5221"\w* \w and he|strong="H1732"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, “\w I have sinned|strong="H2398"\w* \w greatly|strong="H3966"\w* \w in what|strong="H834"\w* \w I have done|strong="H6213"\w*. \w Now|strong="H6258"\w*, \w O LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w I beg You|strong="H4994"\w* \w to take away|strong="H5674"\w* \w the iniquity|strong="H5771"\w* \w of Your servant|strong="H5650"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w I have acted very|strong="H3966"\w* \w foolishly|strong="H5528"\w*.”
\p \v 11 \w When David|strong="H1732"\w* \w got up|strong="H6965"\w* \w in the morning|strong="H1242"\w*, \w the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had come|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Gad|strong="H1410"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H5030"\w*, \w David’s|strong="H1732"\w* \w seer|strong="H2374"\w*: \v 12 “\w Go|strong="H1980"\w* \w and tell|strong="H1696"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w that this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: ‘\w I|strong="H595"\w* \w am offering|strong="H5190"\w* \w you three options|strong="H7969"\w*. \w Choose|strong="H977"\w* \w one|strong="H259"\w* of them, \w and I will carry it out|strong="H6213"\w* against you.’”
\p \v 13 \w So Gad|strong="H1410"\w* \w went|strong="H935"\w* \w and said|strong="H5046"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w*, “\w Do you choose to endure|strong="H935"\w* \w three|strong="H7651"\w*\f + \fr 24:13 \ft LXX (see also \ref 1 Chronicles 21:12|1CH 21:12\ref*); Hebrew \fqa seven\f* \w years|strong="H8141"\w* \w of famine|strong="H7458"\w* \w in your land|strong="H776"\w*, \w three|strong="H7969"\w* \w months|strong="H2320"\w* \w of fleeing|strong="H5127"\w* \w the pursuit|strong="H7291"\w* \w of|strong="H6440"\w* \w your enemies|strong="H6862"\w*, \w or|strong="H518"\w* \w three|strong="H7969"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w of|strong="H1961"\w* \w plague|strong="H1698"\w* \w upon your land|strong="H776"\w*? \w Now then|strong="H6258"\w*, \w think it over|strong="H3045"\w* \w and decide|strong="H7200"\w* \w how|strong="H4100"\w* \w I should reply|strong="H1697"\w* \w to Him who sent me|strong="H7971"\w*.”
\p \v 14 \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w answered|strong="H559"\w* \w Gad|strong="H1410"\w*, “I am \w deeply|strong="H3966"\w* \w distressed|strong="H6862"\w*. \w Please|strong="H4994"\w*, \w let us fall|strong="H5307"\w* \w into the hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w His mercies are|strong="H7356"\w* \w great|strong="H7227"\w*; \w but do not|strong="H408"\w* \w let me fall|strong="H5307"\w* \w into the hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w of men|strong="H120"\w*.”
\s1 A Plague on Israel
\r (\ref 1 Chronicles 21:14–17|1CH 21:14-17\ref*)
\p \v 15 \w So the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w sent|strong="H5414"\w* \w a plague|strong="H1698"\w* \w upon Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w from that morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w the appointed|strong="H4150"\w* \w time|strong="H6256"\w*, \w and seventy|strong="H7657"\w* \w thousand|strong="H505"\w* \w of the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w Dan|strong="H1835"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w Beersheba|strong="H884"\w* \w died|strong="H4191"\w*.\f + \fr 24:15 \ft Literally \fqa and of the people from Dan to Beersheba, seventy thousand men died\f*
\p \v 16 \w But when the angel|strong="H4397"\w* \w stretched|strong="H7971"\w* \w out his hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w to destroy|strong="H7843"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*, \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w relented|strong="H5162"\w* \w from|strong="H413"\w* \w the calamity|strong="H7451"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w* \w to the angel|strong="H4397"\w* \w who was destroying|strong="H7843"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*, “\w Enough|strong="H7227"\w*! \w Withdraw|strong="H7503"\w* \w your hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w now|strong="H6258"\w*!” \w At that time the angel|strong="H4397"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w was|strong="H1961"\w* \w by|strong="H5973"\w* \w the threshing floor|strong="H1637"\w* \w of Araunah|strong="H728"\w*\f + \fr 24:16 \fqa Araunah \ft is a variant of \fqa Ornan\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 21:15|1CH 21:15\ref* and 2 Chronicles 3:1.\f* \w the Jebusite|strong="H2983"\w*.
\p \v 17 \w When David|strong="H1732"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w the angel|strong="H4397"\w* \w striking down|strong="H5221"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w he said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, “\w Surely|strong="H2009"\w* \w I, the shepherd|strong="H595"\w*,\f + \fr 24:17 \ft DSS and LXX; MT does not include \fqa the shepherd\ft .\f* \w have sinned|strong="H2398"\w* \w and|strong="H595"\w* \w acted wickedly|strong="H5753"\w*. \w But these|strong="H428"\w* \w sheep|strong="H6629"\w*, \w what|strong="H4100"\w* \w have they done|strong="H6213"\w*? \w Please|strong="H4994"\w*, \w let Your hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w fall upon|strong="H1961"\w* me \w and my father’s|strong="H1"\w* \w house|strong="H1004"\w*.”
\s1 David Builds an Altar
\r (\ref 1 Chronicles 21:18–30|1CH 21:18-30\ref*)
\p \v 18 \w And that|strong="H1931"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w Gad|strong="H1410"\w* \w came|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w* to him, “\w Go up|strong="H5927"\w* \w and build|strong="H6965"\w* \w an altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w on the threshing floor|strong="H1637"\w* \w of Araunah|strong="H728"\w* \w the Jebusite|strong="H2983"\w*.” \v 19 \w So David|strong="H1732"\w* \w went up|strong="H5927"\w* \w at the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of Gad|strong="H1410"\w*, \w just as|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w*.
\p \v 20 \w When Araunah|strong="H728"\w* \w looked out|strong="H8259"\w* \w and saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and his servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w coming|strong="H5674"\w* \w toward him|strong="H5921"\w*, \w he|strong="H728"\w* \w went out|strong="H3318"\w* \w and bowed|strong="H7812"\w* \w facedown|strong="H639"\w* \w before the king|strong="H4428"\w*. \v 21 “\w Why|strong="H4069"\w* \w has my lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w come|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w his servant|strong="H5650"\w*?” \w Araunah|strong="H728"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w*.
\p “\w To buy|strong="H7069"\w* \w your threshing floor|strong="H1637"\w*,” \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w that I may build|strong="H1129"\w* \w an altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w so that the plague|strong="H4046"\w* \w upon|strong="H5921"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w may be halted|strong="H6113"\w*.”
\p \v 22 \w Araunah|strong="H728"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w*, “\w May my lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w take|strong="H3947"\w* \w whatever seems|strong="H7200"\w* \w good|strong="H2896"\w* \w to him|strong="H5869"\w* \w and offer it up|strong="H5927"\w*. \w Here are the oxen|strong="H1241"\w* \w for a burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w and the threshing sledges|strong="H4173"\w* \w and ox|strong="H1241"\w* \w yokes|strong="H3627"\w* \w for the wood|strong="H6086"\w*. \v 23 \w O king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w Araunah|strong="H728"\w* \w gives|strong="H5414"\w* \w all these|strong="H3605"\w* \w to the king|strong="H4428"\w*.” \w He also|strong="H728"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, “\w May the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w your God|strong="H430"\w* \w accept you|strong="H7521"\w*.”
\p \v 24 “\w No|strong="H3808"\w*,” \w replied|strong="H559"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, “\w I insist on paying|strong="H7069"\w* \w a price|strong="H4242"\w*, \w for I will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w offer|strong="H5927"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w my God|strong="H430"\w* \w burnt offerings|strong="H5930"\w* \w that cost me nothing|strong="H2600"\w*.”
\p \w So David|strong="H1732"\w* \w bought|strong="H7069"\w* \w the threshing floor|strong="H1637"\w* \w and the oxen|strong="H1241"\w* \w for fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w shekels|strong="H8255"\w* \w of silver|strong="H3701"\w*.\f + \fr 24:24 \fqa 50 shekels \ft is approximately 1.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of silver.\f* \v 25 \w And|strong="H1732"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w* \w he built|strong="H1129"\w* \w an altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w and offered|strong="H5927"\w* \w burnt offerings|strong="H5930"\w* \w and peace offerings|strong="H8002"\w*.
\p \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w answered the prayers|strong="H6279"\w* \w on behalf of the land|strong="H776"\w*, \w and the plague|strong="H4046"\w* \w upon|strong="H5921"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w was halted|strong="H6113"\w*.
